{"id": "EUVD-2026-71422", "enisaUuid": "3ba2a8eb-807a-3b6c-b798-75dcd362795b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/ionic: avoid OOB TX partner lookup for hwstamp RXQ\n\nThe dedicated hardware timestamp RX queue is allocated with q->index\nequal to lif->ionic->nrxqs_per_lif. The normal txqcqs array only\ncontains the regular queue pairs, so using that index to set rxq->partner\ncan read one entry past txqcqs[] and then write through the derived\npointer.\nOnly link RX/TX partners for normal queue-pair indexes. Leave the hwstamp\nRX queue unpaired, and make the XDP_TX path abort cleanly if an RX queue\nhas no TX partner.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/881a805a8029ba48c0ce81c6674910f8d83f7afb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39fc615e355b65b8d43be30da57aa95ae6eaf688", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3868046e8e2e761d4d943a232bd109ff22a7d5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea081b4435515ac7177eb598a3c0678d1b9e7911", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d92255b405fb6f5acca408239ccd742e0a42c9cb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5565-rhhw-mpqw", "CVE-2026-80779"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3853c525-b3ae-3aa3-8258-8fa805797b41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "5e2c6611-c78e-36e1-99be-8a83180a5c4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8eeed8373e1cca836799bf8e4a05cffa8e444908 <39fc615e355b65b8d43be30da57aa95ae6eaf688"}, {"id": "5e5c64a6-5b01-3c34-b5c5-a11dc11cd3dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "73a9e7af-f533-3161-8d9b-ef0f52944971", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.47"}, {"id": "87d8db31-bfb5-3822-995d-c8e967d4a654", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":